WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:06.000
This video is about what may need to be done with service videos after they have been live streamed to YouTube.

00:06.000 --> 00:14.000
When a service is streamed on YouTube, people can watch it live, and the video is also saved on the church's YouTube channel for later viewing.

00:14.000 --> 00:20.000
This is all done automatically by the Streamlabs software on the streaming computer at the church.

00:21.000 --> 00:24.000
Sometimes, there may not be anything that needs to be changed.

00:24.000 --> 00:35.000
If the person running the live stream displays the YouTube title slide that is prepared prior to the service, there is a chance that YouTube will pick that slide as the thumbnail slide for the service video.

00:35.000 --> 00:42.000
However, often this title slide will need to be set up manually in YouTube, and there may be further adjustments needed.

00:43.000 --> 00:48.000
First, let's take a look at how people can get to the service videos on the church's YouTube channel.

00:48.000 --> 00:52.000
From the church website, you select, listen, and then services.

01:00.000 --> 01:04.000
In the past live streams section, we can see some of the latest services.

01:07.000 --> 01:11.000
The first two videos here have not been updated after the service was streamed.

01:11.000 --> 01:18.000
You can see that they do not have a title slide for the videos, like the third slide shown with a slide for epiphany.

01:21.000 --> 01:24.000
Also, these two videos both have the same title.

01:24.000 --> 01:30.000
The title was not changed properly when the live stream was started on the service that followed the epiphany service.

01:32.000 --> 01:38.000
There is another problem with the service that is second from the left, that unfortunately we cannot fix in YouTube.

01:38.000 --> 01:47.000
This is not a common problem. It appears there was a problem with how the live stream software was capturing the video, and the picture appears shifted slightly to the left.

01:47.000 --> 01:52.000
This problem has since been fixed so that future live streams should not have this problem.

01:54.000 --> 01:58.000
Next, let's confirm what the titles of the latest two videos should be.

01:58.000 --> 02:05.000
If the one titled Second Sunday of Epiphany is correct, the previous one is probably First Sunday of Epiphany.

02:05.000 --> 02:08.000
But we will take a look at the Planning Center website to make sure.

02:09.000 --> 02:13.000
Login to Planning Center using your personal account.

02:14.000 --> 02:18.000
There are multiple ways to get to the different services in Planning Center.

02:18.000 --> 02:23.000
Here we will use the master calendar to get to the Sunday service after Epiphany.

02:30.000 --> 02:34.000
We will click on the Sunday morning services link on the Sunday after Epiphany.

02:36.000 --> 02:42.000
At the top, we can see that this Sunday is in fact the first Sunday of Epiphany.

02:43.000 --> 02:48.000
Let's also verify the title of the next Sunday by clicking the right arrow near the top.

02:51.000 --> 02:55.000
And now we see, the next Sunday is the second Sunday.

02:57.000 --> 03:02.000
While we're in the Planning Center website, let's get the title slides for those two Sundays.

03:02.000 --> 03:09.000
The YouTube title slide for a service should be attached as a file in the Plan Files section at the bottom left.

03:10.000 --> 03:15.000
The title slide can be previewed and downloaded so that we can set the title slide on YouTube.

03:19.000 --> 03:22.000
We will save the file to our computer.

03:23.000 --> 03:27.000
Now let's go back to the first Sunday and get its title slides.

03:27.000 --> 03:30.000
We save that file, and now we have both the slides we need.

03:32.000 --> 03:36.000
Next, let's look at how we can work with the videos within the Church's YouTube channel.

03:38.000 --> 03:42.000
Now let's go back to the first Sunday and get its title slide too.

03:47.000 --> 03:51.000
We save that file, and now we have both the slides we need.

03:52.000 --> 03:56.000
Next, let's look at how we can work with the videos within the Church's YouTube channel.

03:57.000 --> 04:00.000
Login to YouTube with the Church's Google account.

04:03.000 --> 04:07.000
Then, select Your Videos from the menu on the left side.

04:14.000 --> 04:18.000
At the top, under Channel Content, select Live.

04:19.000 --> 04:25.000
Here we see those recent videos again, and we can also see the date each video was streamed.

04:26.000 --> 04:29.000
This can help us make sure we are updating the correct videos.

04:31.000 --> 04:34.000
Let's work on fixing up the video for the January 11 service.

04:35.000 --> 04:39.000
It needs to have the title text changed, and also the title slide added.

04:43.000 --> 04:46.000
When you use the mouse to hover over the text,

04:46.000 --> 04:50.000
next to the video, Options for working with the video appear.

04:51.000 --> 04:55.000
We will select the pencil icon, which lets us modify details about the video.

05:01.000 --> 05:03.000
First, let's change the title text.

05:04.000 --> 05:06.000
This can be edited near the top of the page.

05:16.000 --> 05:30.000
Next, we will upload the title slide we got from Planning Center as the thumbnail for the video.

05:31.000 --> 05:34.000
Click on Upload File in the thumbnail section.

05:38.000 --> 05:41.000
Select the file downloaded from Planning Center.

05:46.000 --> 05:55.000
Now we see, in the upper right part of the screen, that the thumbnail has been replaced with the title slide.

05:56.000 --> 06:00.000
Next, click the Save button to save the changes we have made.

06:01.000 --> 06:05.000
Then, click Channel Content to return to the list of videos.

06:05.000 --> 06:17.000
Next, we will fix up the video for January 18 by selecting the Details icon, next to it.

06:25.000 --> 06:29.000
All we need to do here, is upload the title slide for the video's thumbnail.

06:35.000 --> 06:48.000
Then, we save the changes and return to the channel content.

06:48.000 --> 07:11.000
Now we see that the two latest videos have the correct text for the titles, and the thumbnails are set to the correct title slides.

07:12.000 --> 07:20.000
Next, let's check how the channel looks to everyone else by clicking, your channel.

07:24.000 --> 07:28.000
Select the Live option to see the latest live stream videos.

07:28.000 --> 07:41.000
Everything looks good here. And that should be all we need to do to get the latest live stream videos set up properly, in YouTube.

